Market Challenges
Handling radioactive precursors requires strict radiation protection procedures, qualified personnel and validated facilities. Maintaining consistent quality records and coordinating shipments across different regulatory jurisdictions can also increase operational complexity.

Market Restraints
Integrated isotope suppliers may retain processing, quality and distribution activities within their own operations, limiting the addressable market for independent service providers. High licensing costs, specialist staffing requirements and lengthy clinical development timelines can further constrain service expansion.

